    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm just trying to visualize the whole \"defense\" aspect. If we think of these gates as a line of protection, are there specific ways these errors or \"bugs\" manage to slip through even when we think we have everything covered? Like, what's the profile of a failure that actually manages to bypass a well-configured gate?",
