    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Bugs that slip through are often the ones that are *not* in the test suite, which is a common pitfall—like a very specific, rare combination of user actions that only happens under high load. These are often \"integration\" or \"environmental\" failures, not simple syntax errors. A failure might also be related to how the application interacts with external services, which is hard to perfectly mock in automated tests. Think of it as a small, highly specialized, and surprisingly complex corner case that only a very specific, rare, and highly motivated (or unlucky) user will trigger.",
      "source": "target",
